    max_records: int = Field(10, cli=("-m", "--max-records"))
    min_filter_score: float = Field(..., cli=("-f", "--filter-score"))", "replace": "    input_file: str = Field(..., json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-i", "--input")})
    max_records: int = Field(10, json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-m", "--max-records")})
    min_filter_score: float = Field(
        ..., json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-f", "--filter-score")}
    )", "explanation": "Pydantic V2 deprecates passing arbitrary keyword arguments (such as `cli=`) directly to `Field`; per the V2 migration guide, extra metadata must be supplied via `json_schema_extra`. The `cli` value is moved into a `json_schema_extra` dict under the same key, so the stored metadata and CLI behavior are unchanged. The `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` migration already present in the file is left intact."}], "notes": "The previous attempt already converted `class Config` to `model_config = ConfigDict(...)`, so that part is correct and kept. The remaining failure is the deprecated extra keyword `cli=` passed to `Field` on three fields (input_file, max_records, min_filter_score); these are moved into `json_schema_extra={"cli": ...}`. The keys and tuple values are unchanged. No import changes are needed, since `Field` and `ConfigDict` are already imported. Not verified by running the tests. `alpha` and `values` have no Field calls and need no change."}
